\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. From Greenland's icy mountains,
\par From India's coral strand, 
\par Where Afric's sunny fountains
\par Roll down their golden sand,
\par From many an ancient river, 
\par From many a palmy plain,
\par They call us to deliver
\par Their land from error's chain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Can we, who souls are lighted
\par Wih wisdom from on high,
\par Can we to men benighted
\par The lamp of life deny?
\par Salvation! O salvation!
\par The joyful sound proclaim
\par Till each remotest nation
\par Has learned Messiah's name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Waft, waft, ye winds, His story,
\par And you, ye waters, roll, 
\par Till, like a sea of glory,
\par It spreads from pole to pole;
\par Till o'er are ransomed nature,
\par The Lamb for sinners slain,
\par Redeemer, King, creator,
\par In bliss returns to reign.
\par Amen.
\par 
\par  \f1 
